  "query_preview": "..\nIssued 1057 PM CDT Wed Sep 30 2026\n\nFriday through Wednesday:\n\nThe models have fairly good agreement for the overall pattern\nthis weekend into next week. Nly winds and weakening cold \nadvection will prevail on Fri followed by high pressure around \n1027 mb for Fri nt. After a relatively cool day in the lower \n60s, low temps will fall into the middle 30s to lower 40s inland\nfrom the lake. Patchy frost will be possible around sunrise Sat\nnorth of Madison.\n\nA west to northwesterly flow aloft will prevail for the weekend\ninto the middle of next week. A shortwave trough and sfc low\nwill track across the Canadian border over the Great Plains on\nSat, with the low to deepen and track into central Ontario for \nSat nt. Sly winds and warm advection will return to srn WI\nfollowed by a dry cold front Sun AM. High temps will warm \nthrough the 60s for the weekend.\n\nA surface ridge will pass on Mon followed by another low across\ncentral Canada bringing sly winds to srn WI on Tue. Relatively\ncool temps on Mon will warm a bit for Tue, followed by another\ncold front and upper trough passage on Wed. There is uncertainty\non whether this front will be a dry passage, but the forecast is\ndry at this time. \n\nGehring",
